    "body": "## Integrated change\n\nAdd bounded occurrence admission to the same Rust recurrent graph used by full-sequence learning and incremental generation. Policies include the selected orthant64 proposer and full/recent64/recent32/exact-cache controls. Preserve causal read-before-write, exact occurrence ages and copy identity, selected language gradients, NoRead, packed policy binding, fixed-grid continuation and resumable optimizer/data clocks. Incremental bounded reads fetch selected event tensors; offline dense layouts remain explicit.\n\n## Executed decision\n\nBoth orthant64 arms complete the fixed256-update B16/T256 continuation from the retained learned-code parents. **Both fail source retention and are not promoted.** Frozen gate vectors: PASS/PASS/PASS/FAIL/PASS.\n\n| Metric | Quaternion | Householder pair |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Final bounded NLL | 2.129595124 | 2.124890468 |\n| Gap against own accepted hard parent | +0.015368955 | +0.014010668 |\n| Complete source answers, parent → candidate | 28 → 17 /32 | 24 → 17 /32 |\n| Prior first-noun losses, maximum2 | 11 | 8 |\n| Same final weights, recent64 complete answers | 27 /32 | 25 /32 |\n\nThe indexed complement contributes17 complete answers over recent32 and passes its separate utility discriminator. Same-weights full/recent64 recovery identifies substantial policy loss; exact-cache is also inferior to recent64 here. Accepted learned-code parents and all negatives remain preserved. Next is one matched recent64 continuation using existing source and fixed recipe; longer-range geometric admission needs explicit candidate-recall credit. No policy override is silently promoted.\n\nThe64 cap counts admitted events. Training and evaluation both retain256-token contexts. One paired seed on exposed development; no final holdout or checkpoint reselection.\n\n## Validation and resources\n\n- 62 focused optimized Rust checks PASS in4.79seconds; release build PASS. Actual packed reload probability delta zero and seeded token/distribution parity in both arms.\n- 16 prescribed model evaluations complete; principal arithmetic verifies44 sealed input roots,58 binding records, every target record and preserved source changes.\n- Three DeepSeek sessions through RDC, with independent principal adjudication. Two local Rust fits concurrent on this M1; two sequence workers/model, backend threads1. No Kimi or external training hardware.\n- Paired training wall24.67minutes, build/check compilation7.55minutes. Original reserve checkpoint at166+exact90-update resume; actual segment sample hashes match. Prospective512MiB storage allowance preserves14.5GiB reserve plus128MiB stop and64MiB closeout. No deletions.\n- Formatting and claim-wording PASS; committed-range whitespace check PASS after trimming16 trailing spaces in the Markdown output display. Exact JSON strings and sealed outputs remain unchanged.\n- Five queue statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not executed tests. Final serving arithmetic is still F32/dense; no general language, geometric advantage, Hamiltonian dynamics, D5 sparsity or energy qualification.\n\n## Evidence and current direction\n\nSee `docs/integration/bounded-admission-result-2026-09-25.md`, its prospective plan, complete outputs, decision/recipe/review/resource receipts, and updated README/current-state/canonical ladder/source map/evidence index/training README. Executed Rust source is78fde5711ea01f80783eb9911e01197a61406d1a; subsequent commits change documentation only. Cumulative accounting includes preparation, all reviews, build, stops, learning, evaluation and delivery.\n\nReferences #973\nReferences #820\n",
